            <p>A Greenland cruise transports you to one of the most remote and spectacular places on earth. Greenland is famous for its massive icebergs, deep fjords, colorful settlements, and untouched nature. There's no better way to explore this Arctic wonder than by ship, especially as some of its most staggering sights can only truly be accessed from the sea. </p>

            <p>Selecting a cruise to Greenland provides the traveler with access to massive glaciers, floating ice sculpture and the serene wildness of the Arctic in high style. Once ships pass towering ice cliffs and travel through deep blue waters, it is all overwhelming in scale. Every day is a discovery with nature at the forefront. </p>

            <h2>Cruise to Greenland Scenic Highlights</h2>

            <p>Port calls during cruises to Greenland typically include stops at some of its fjords, whose waters are so peaceful that icebergs are able to float through them. Travellers can watch the glaciers crack off into the sea, sounding like thunder rolling across the land. Little coastal villages contribute spiritual richness to the passage, with colorful wooden cottages providing contrast against snow-clad scenery. </p>

            <p>A browser that's too chilly (albeit not as cold as it was to start) or an eternal search for puffins are just a few of the perils and pleasures awaiting you when you go on a cruise to Greenland. Travelers may see the ghosts of whales surfacing near the ship, seabirds soaring in the sky above, and, once in a while,e seals lounging on bits of ice. It is the mix of creatures and awesome sights that brings the Arctic alive and memorable. </p>

            <h2>Iceland and Greenland Cruises Combined Trip Choices</h2>

            <p>You can also take longer cruises to Iceland and Greenland if you want a more expansive Arctic adventure. These trips usually start in Iceland, then cross the Denmark Strait to Greenland's rugged coast. The contrast is stark between Iceland's volcanic vistas and Greenland's icy fjords. </p>

            <p>On Iceland and Greenland cruises, passengers take in geysers and waterfalls in Iceland before voyaging on to vast glaciers and remote Arctic villages of Greenland. This two-destination trip allows for further exploration of northern cultures and the natural world while on one continuous journey. </p>

            <h2>Silversea Greenland Luxury Exploration</h2>

            <p><a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/silversea-cruises">Silversea</a> Greenland cruises pair arctic adventures with a sense of personal and intimate wellbeing. Similar trips run by Silversea Cruises also incorporate smaller vessels built for polar travel. For guests, the experience includes spacious suites, attentive service, and expert guides offering insight into the history and wildlife of the region. </p>

            <p>A silver wind Greenland journey is also a feeling of relaxed summer life and exploration. After a day of activities (like zodiac trips in icebergs), passengers return to gourmet meals and relaxing lounges. This blend of exploratory and luxury resonates with travelers who don't want to skimp on comfort or authenticity. </p>

            <h2>Hurtigruten Greenland Expedition Style</h2>

            <p>Hurtigruten ice greenland sailings specialise in an expedition-based cruise. Hurtigruten prides itself on sustainability and education, and provides immersive experiences led by naturalists who have been in the business for years. The ships are constructed to handle Arctic waters, all while being environmentally friendly. </p>

            <p>On Hurtigruten Greenland, travelers also take part in shore landings and educational lectures that help to heighten their knowledge of climate and culture. They are always about more than just eye candy, so no matter what you do at Secrets, it feels like something special instead of just a place to fill your drinks tab. </p>

            <h2>Other Cruise Lines that Cruise to the Arctic</h2>

            <p>Few cruise lines offer dedicated circumnavigation of Greenland itineraries; specialist expedition operators dominate in that market. And other brands may feature Arctic navigation as part of a broader northern European voyage (although there, too, we ran across a few suitable slots). Lines like <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/cunard-cruise-line">Cunard Line</a> and <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/holland-america-cruises">Holland America Line</a> will sometimes have itineraries to the north that skim by Arctic waters. Luxury players, including <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/regent-seven-seas-cruise-line">Regent Seven Seas</a> and <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/seabourn-cruise-line">Seabourn Cruise Line</a>, may also have a few select sailings.</p>

            <p>Arctic expeditions are still a niche, in part because most of the mainstream lines, such as <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/royal-caribbean-cruises">Royal Caribbean</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/msc-cruise-line">MSC Cruises</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/carnival-cruise-line">Carnival Cruise Line</a>, and <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/norwegian-cruise-line">Norwegian Cruise Line</a>, focus almost exclusively on warm-weather destinations. This narrow focus is what helps conserve the fragile nature of Greenland while also offering very high-quality birding. </p>

            <h2>Life At Sea During an Arctic Cruise</h2>

            <p>Life aboard a floating to Greenland is all about seeing and contemplating. Lounge decks and open terraces enable guests to view ice formations and evolving light as darkness segues into dawn. The onboard atmosphere is generally serene, and lectures and discussions will add a level of enrichment to your journey. </p>

            <p>The Arctic sky changes color, and quiet moments of appreciation come late in the evening. And at certain times of year, visitors may even get to see the northern lights dancing across the skyline. The vessel is a cozy base amidst all the drama and sometimes unpredictable weather of the Arctic. </p>

